\description{
Extracts \strong{ERA5-Land} climate variables for a user-defined region
and time range from the Earth Engine datasets
\strong{ECMWF/ERA5_LAND/DAILY_AGGR} (\code{by = "daily"}) or
\strong{ECMWF/ERA5_LAND/MONTHLY_AGGR} (\code{by = "month"}), plus
\strong{ECMWF/ERA5_LAND/HOURLY} for the diurnal bands \code{"rh_day"}/\code{"rh_night"}.
Each image is summarized over the region using a chosen
statistic (e.g., mean/median), values are converted to conventional
units (degrees Celsius, mm, volume fraction), and the function
returns an \code{sf} or \code{tibble}.

ERA5-Land is the land-component replay of the ECMWF ERA5 climate
reanalysis (Copernicus Climate Data Store), with global coverage
from 1950 to near-present at ~9 km (0.1 degrees) resolution.
It complements \code{l4h_chirps()} (finer precipitation) and
\code{l4h_terra_climate()} (finer monthly climatology) by providing
\strong{daily} exposure windows and soil-moisture variables that are
key for vector-borne disease modelling (temperature/precipitation lags).

